  "problem": "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $10?$\n\n- ${R}_{10}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{5}(R)$, the vector space of all $5\\times 5$ matrices over $R$\n- ${R}^{10}$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11\\ne 10.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(\\text{R}))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{5}(R))={5}^{2}=25\\ne 10.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{10})=10.\\,\u2713\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
